    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440-a20">

                <pb facs="0415" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg341"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>

                <head>Mr. Bigelow to Mr. Mongel Bey</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 18, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">President:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of the letter of the international committee for establishing the
                    American canal by the isthmus of Darien over which you preside. You will much
                    oblige me by transmitting to your colleagues my thanks for the sympathy whereof
                    you send me so precious tokens, on the occasion of our great national mourning.
                    I take pleasure in assuring you of the interest I feel in the success of
                    enterprises which, like yours, are dest ned to render more easy the
                    communication between different portions of the American continent, and by
                    consequence to draw more close the ties of amity which unite their
                    inhabitants.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the expressions of my most distinguished sentiments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mongel Bey.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
